      {
        "name": "DTI/Fault/Fault_Code",
        "unit": "",
        "doc": "Fault code",
        "desc": "0x00 : NO FAULTS\n0x01 : Overvoltage - The input voltage is higher than the set maximum.\n0x02 : Undervoltage - The input voltage is lower than the set minimum.\n0x03 : DRV - Transistor or transistor drive error\n0x04 : ABS. Overcurrent - The AC current is higher than the set absolute maximum current. \n0x05 : CTLR Overtemp. - The controller temperature is higher than the set maximum.\n0x06 : Motor Overtemp. - The motor temperature is higher than the set maximum.\n0x07 : Sensor wire fault - Something went wrong with the sensor differential signals.\n0x08 : Sensor general fault - An error occurred while processing the sensor signals\n0x09 : CAN Command error - CAN message received contains parameter out of boundaries\n0x0A : Analog input error – Redundant output out of range",
        "values": [
          3
        ]
      }
    ],
    "sim_freq": 25
